  "rationale": "Initial baseline, 0.5.0: the committed twenty-year gate baseline for the agent-interface release. These numbers are a measurement and not a balance claim -- release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0, and 0.5.0 is the release that builds the instrument rather than one that tunes the game. Nothing moved: all ten values are identical to the decimal against the baseline this supersedes, because agent-interface's closeout added an arm-scoped metric layer written beside a run record that reads nothing the simulation did not already compute. The universe these vital signs describe is still degenerate in ways that are named rather than hidden: all 200 gated runs are the passive control, which submits no god verb, so god-agency's verbs are installed and unexercised here; library depth sits near 1.7 distinct nodes against 525 grimoires because the scribable list is cost-ordered and the same cheap nodes are copied over and over; and several observation channels saturate. This is the gate that reads whether the universe stopped -- referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter at 0.66 nodes over the final five years says it has nearly, at 48.35 of the 51 v1 nodes.",
